immy's  personality in the prequel  francesca also plays a role in the  reintroduction of the final return  character in season three when she goes  out into the hall to bring huel babino  into the courtroom in one of my  all-time favorite better call saul  episodes chicanery  of course we'd already seen him show up  bumping into chuck on the stairs to  plant the cell phone battery  we first saw huel on screen in the  premiere episode of breaking bad season  4. from there he becomes a regular in  saul's story  and he brings to mind the character  patrick qb  these two work together a lot and qb is  one of the characters that's yet to make  a return  although i think the part that steven  ogg played in season 5 was written for  him  only bill burr wasn't available to  reprise the role  the fourth season to better call saul  only has a few characters that return  nick was a part of gus's security team  in breaking bad  he makes a couple of appearances in that  series with the first coming in season 4  episode  7. he doesn't last long in his run there  though  and better call saul nick first appears  in the second episode of the fourth  season  in a blink and you'd miss him situation  where he's holding a gun on  nacho as the season continues he has  several other appearances  the other two return character scenes in  this season come in the third  episode something beautiful first we  have ira who we met as the owner of  vamanos pest in the third  episode of breaking bad season five in  his better call  saul debut he's hired by jimmy to steal  the hummel figurine from mr neff's  office  while he's stuck there we get another  reference to walt throwing the pizza on  the roof of his house  to get that shot the crew had to use a  pie that wasn't pre-sliced  fans noticed that and it led to a big  discussion for why walt would have  bought a pizza like that  the writers addressed this in the next  season when badger tells jesse that they  don't cut their pizzas  and pass the savings on to you in bcs  when neff orders his pizza we hear him  confirm on the phone that he wants it  pre-sliced and when it arrives we see  the boxes the same it's from venezia's  gail bettiker is the second return  character in this episode  he first appeared in the sixth episode  of breaking bad's third season  in a short stint as walt's new assistant  in the super lab  he pretty much got the short end of the  stick at every turn in the original  series  so it was nice to see him return in bcs  when gus needed his expertise  the first returning character in the  most recent fifth season  is a special one edgal braith aka  ed the disappearer is one of only two  characters that have shown up in  breaking bad  better call saul and the el camino movie  up into this point  do you know who the other one is ed  didn't make his breaking bad debut  until the penultimate episode of that  series and he only showed up in that one  episode  his services were mentioned several  times before that but we only see him in  granite state  he plays a considerable role in el  camino which is some of the last acting  work he did as he lost his battle with  brain cancer and passed away  on the same day the movie was released  he does appear  in the better call saul season 5 teaser  when he gets a call from gene  after he gets spooked by jeff the cab  driver they were able to pull this  off by shooting his bcs scene during the  filming of el camino  the timing of this turned out to be a  lucky break for the prequel series  because even before his passing they  thought it might be too difficult to  rebuild the vacuum cleaner store  and fly him to albuquerque for just that  phone call  he probably wouldn't have shown up on  screen in the fifth season if it didn't  play out this way  so rest in peace to robert forrester  there are two minor characters that  return in season five although  the first jody nichols was portrayed by  two different actors in her appearances  she debuted in breaking bad way back in  the seventh episode of the first season  as the realtor who was trying to sell  jessie's house and better call saul the  new actor played the character as she  was holding an open house that jimmy and  kim visit  in the second episode we also saw the  return of detective tim roberts  he had his breaking bad debut in the  second episode of the second  season investigating walt's  disappearance  in bcs he makes his debut in episode 6  of season 5  after mike makes sure some evidence  about lalo's car lands on his desk  peter shuler is a character that had a  short but memorable arc in the second  episode of the fifth season of breaking  bad he goes from taste testing sauces to  committing suicide by shocking himself  with an automated external defibrillator  he accomplished this by sticking one end  in his mouth and one over his heart  and after he hits the deck that toilet  keeps auto flushing  we see him in happier times in a meeting  of important people from madrigal's  restaurant chains later he meets with  gus and lydia in a hotel room where  there's reference to a time in santiago  where their backs were against the wall  this connects peter to gus's mysterious  past in chile  and may hint that we could learn more  about that in saul's final season  probably the most anticipated character  returns in the fifth season were hank  schrader and steve gomez  hank and gomi made their debut in the  pilot of the original series  and in that first episode they took walt  on a ride along  that made a bus that involved jesse and  emilio  when they make their return and better  call saul we see how crazy8 became one  of their snitches  and how that was all set up by lalo and  that  of course sets things in motion to come  full circle as crazy 8 is the one who  gave them that  tip that led to the bust in breaking  bad's pilot years later  and speaking of full circle that brings  us to the last crossover character the  man with the mustache  he made a couple of appearances in  season 2 and season 4  breaking bad apparently he knew the  actor that played gomi  and he got the job that way but where i  remembered him from was the 10th episode  of season 5  as hank walks past him sitting at a desk  in his office and you can get a good  look at the mustache  he makes his bcs debut in episode 504  as hank's congratulating his men on  their bust at the money drops  that is all 35 of the breaking bad  characters that appear and better call  saul  through the first five seasons i'll just  mention  that lalo and ignacio aka nacho were  mentioned  but never appeared in breaking bad so  they don't make the list  we still have one 13-episode season to  go  which will probably be starting in early  2022  the question i'll leave you with is  which characters are you hoping to see  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already  i'll be doing more better call solve  videos before season 6  gets here and we'll be doing multiple  weekly videos like i did last season  while it's airing  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon
 

